cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "ARCADE-Checkout: robot-learning data for retail checkout, built from real human demonstrations"
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Human data (ARCADE-Checkout-Human): 3-D human hand-object demonstrations at a self-checkout counter (body, hands,
  product 6-DoF pose, grasp/release events, segmentation masks). Robot data (ARCADE-Checkout-FFW-SH5,
  ARCADE-Checkout-UR10e, ARCADE-Checkout-G1): the episodes retargeted to the ROBOTIS FFW-SH5 humanoid,
  to two UR10e arms with Robotiq 2F-140 grippers and to the Unitree G1 humanoid with Dex3-1 hands, in
  LeRobot format.
authors:
  - name: "SpaceVision AI"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SpaceVision-ai/ARCADE-Checkout"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
keywords: [robotics, hand-object interaction, human demonstrations, 6-DoF object pose, humanoid, retargeting, LeRobot, dexterous manipulation, ROBOTIS FFW-SH5, UR10e, Robotiq 2F-140, Unitree G1, Dex3-1, whole-body manipulation, bimanual manipulation, dataset, retail]
